WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.572
Conflict of interest registry.

00:00:02.522 --> 00:00:05.545
Every documented conflict in one page.

00:00:05.545 --> 00:00:12.000
This page consolidates all documented conflicts of interest identified across the TENET5 investigation.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.443
From the PM's Brookfield stock options to the CRTC's revolving door with telecoms.

00:00:17.443 --> 00:00:22.556
From SNC-Lavalin's PMO interference to OSFI regulators from banks.

00:00:22.556 --> 00:00:29.374
Each conflict is sourced from Ethics Commissioner filings, appointment records, corporate filings, or parliamentary testimony.

00:00:29.374 --> 00:00:38.522
Together they form the personnel architecture of institutional capture: the people making decisions have financial or professional ties to the entities affected by those decisions.

00:00:38.522 --> 00:00:41.193
The personnel architecture of capture.

00:00:41.193 --> 00:00:51.590
Every conflict documented on this page follows the same pattern: the person or body making decisions has financial, professional, or structural ties to the entities affected by those decisions.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:56.147
The PM from Brookfield sets MAID policy affecting Brookfield's portfolio.

00:00:56.147 --> 00:01:00.272
CRTC commissioners from telecoms regulate telecoms.

00:01:00.272 --> 00:01:03.272
OSFI from banks regulates banks.

00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:07.454
Senate appointments by the PM review bills that could constrain the PM.

00:01:07.454 --> 00:01:11.818
Pension funds invest everyone's retirement in the system's continuation.

00:01:11.818 --> 00:01:15.068
This is not a collection of individual conflicts.

00:01:15.068 --> 00:01:22.159
It is a documented personnel architecture where every decision-maker has a structural interest in maintaining the captured system.
